{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1234903-what-dark-age-fae-books-do-you-want","id":1234903,"title":"What Dark Age Fae Books do you Want?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-14T03:52:06-07:00","id":1234903,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What Dark Age Fae Books do you Want?","content":"<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So I'm reading Dark Age Fae for the first time and we only really got one book, well one book and a chapter with Darkening Sky. But if you could get more books for Dark Age Fae what would you cover? I think we desperately need a Players guide, to include analogues for the precursors to Houses and Kiths, maybe as a Background or something like a Camp/House in other settings? And maybe ways to represent the Exceptional Fae like the Seasonal Rulers and maybe even a introducing some other Dominions, I know they are supposed to be all encompassing but there could be room... Maybe a Book for each of the Continents/Regions? Like a book covering the Lands of the Hsien, and a Book on India, the Americas and Africa. Perhaps introducing alternate Courts, perhaps borrowing the idea of Directional Courts for Asia, I mean they already use the Seasonal courts from Lost...</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T06:29:24-07:00","id":1234926,"title":"","content":"Player's Guide for sure.<br /> <br /> I think that a book covering more in detail the Seelie-Unseelie split and the Season Court would alsee to have a better feel of how things goes.<br /> <br /> A book covering Europe and detailing some specificity of the Fae there (Norse Fae, Rus Fae, etc.) Would be great too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 07-14-2018, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:45:58-07:00","id":1235004,"title":"","content":"I would love a section/book on the Norse Fae and the Slavic Fae! Maybe include some Baba Yaga interactions!<br /> <br /> A book on the Gods from th Fae Perpective!<br /> <br /> Some talk about less humanoid Fae like Dragons/Wyrms and things like giants too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T14:55:44-07:00","id":1240222,"title":"","content":"A book with more Lesser and Greater features, describing their mechanics, so we can adapt Norse, Slavic, Iberian, etc faeries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T15:08:03-07:00","id":1240227,"title":"","content":"Something talking about how the DA Fae metaphysics become the Changeling the Dreaming metaphysics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T00:10:11-07:00","id":1242637,"title":"","content":"If there had been a Companion book for the original, it'd probably have included expanded Court info, more Treasures and other background goodies, new cantrips, maybe a fifth Solstice dominion, stuff about the medieval Dreaming (maybe), more on the various agendas, and maybe more about the fae in the middle east and Africa. The lack of anything about Asia for Mage means the Hsien would've probably been ignored. I'd enjoy seeing all of the above expanded on.<br /> <br /> I'd honestly enjoy each Court+matching Dominion getting a big fat source book full of strongholds, treasures, sprites, cantrips, regional variations, NPCs, features, examples of real period faerie creatures and stories that fit the court and so on. Book of Winter, Spring, etc.<br /> <br /> Added: Some sort of atlas-type book along the lines of DA: Europe or a series of books about different regions - Scandinavia, France, the British Isles, Greece, etc. - and the fae there - alfar and joten, giants and white ladies, green men and boggarts, lampads and satyrs - with their unique customs and traditions, including how they've dealt with Christianity and other changes (as well as possible relations with local vampires, were beasts, wizards and other things).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 08-04-2018, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T18:29:40-07:00","id":1243085,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if it would be feasible to have a DA:F book that is a bestiary of medieval and classical/ancient faerie beings and templates for how to make them using Features and/or stats for them as followers/pets. Something that's maybe about 25 or so &quot;races&quot; and another 25 or so creatures. Try to spread them out across Europe and the Middle East and evenly between what would seem to fit each Court. <br /> <br /> Hmmm ...<ul><li>Ljosalfar/Dokkalfar</li> <li>Dvergr</li> <li>Jotunn</li> <li>Hulder</li> <li>White Women</li> <li>Rusalka/Nixie/Ondine/Kelpie</li> <li>Satyr/Faun/Glaistig</li> <li>Ogre</li> <li>Boggart/Brownie</li> <li>Dullahan</li> <li>Hag</li> <li>Swan Maid</li> <li>Clurichaun</li> <li>Lampad</li> <li>Amazon</li> <li>Dryad/Green Men/Samodivas</li> <li>Oread</li> <li>Ifrit</li> <li>Peri</li> <li>Ghoul</li> <li>Hamzad</li> <li>Vanara</li> <li>Strigoi</li> <li>Nocnitsa</li> </ul>Or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}